<script>
import askAssistantSource from 'crm/src/assistant/askAssistant.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import askClaudeCodeSource from 'crm/src/assistant/askClaudeCode.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import AssistantThread from 'crm/src/assistant/lib/AssistantThread.abide'
import assistantThreadSource from 'crm/src/assistant/lib/AssistantThread.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import assistantThreadTestSource from 'crm/src/assistant/lib/AssistantThread.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import ClaudeCodeChat from 'crm/src/assistant/lib/ClaudeCodeChat.abide'
import claudeCodeChatSource from 'crm/src/assistant/lib/ClaudeCodeChat.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import claudeCodeChatTestSource from 'crm/src/assistant/lib/ClaudeCodeChat.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import permitClaudeCodeSource from 'crm/src/assistant/permitClaudeCode.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
import Snippet from '#src/lib/Snippet.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="An answer streams into the chat as the assistant writes it">
        <Example
            id="chat-assistant"
            title={"`<Chat ask={askAssistant} />` — the CRM's assistant, as a conversation"}
            summary="A rep asks the CRM's assistant which company Ada is at, and presses Enter. The tool call it makes shows as it runs, then the answer. The model is a recording; the search it calls is the CRM's own handler."
            files={{
                'src/assistant/lib/AssistantThread.abide': assistantThreadSource,
                'src/assistant/askAssistant.handler.ts': askAssistantSource,
                'src/assistant/lib/AssistantThread.test.ts': assistantThreadTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <AssistantThread />
        </Example>

        <p><code>ask</code> is your assistant handler, the <code>POST</code> that yields
            <code>assistant</code>'s events. <code>Chat</code> calls it with every turn so far
            and reads the events as they stream. The handler keeps nothing between calls, so its
            address, its middleware and its tools stay yours.</p>

        <p>Enter sends and Shift+Enter starts a new line. An Enter that picks a word in an input
            method does neither. An image pasted into the composer, or dropped on it, goes with
            the next question, drawn by <code>imagePiece</code>. While the answer streams, Stop
            replaces Send: it aborts the call, and the answer keeps what had arrived.</p>

        <p>The assistant's words render as plain text. Hand a component taking
            <code>text</code> as <code>Text</code> to render them another way, as markdown for
            one. The transcript follows its bottom as the answer grows, until the reader scrolls
            up, and again once they scroll back down.</p>

        <p><code>Chat</code> holds the conversation as <code>AssistantTurn</code>s, and the
            <code>transcript</code> functions it folds them with are yours for a chat laid out
            some other way. Fold each event once, as it arrives, inside the
            <code>patch</code> of the reactive value holding the turns. Words join the words
            before them, so a chunk rewrites one text node. Folding every event again per chunk
            costs the square of the answer's length, and the chat's test counts the reads to hold
            it to one per event.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>You write</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>transcript.turn('assistant')</code></td><td>a turn with every field set, for a question you build or an answer to fold into</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>transcript.fold(answering, event)</code></td><td>one event folded into its turn in place: words joined, a tool call paired with its input and its result by id, a permission prompt waiting, <code>done</code> setting <code>stop</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>transcript.messages(turns)</code></td><td>the turns as an assistant handler takes them, leaving out an answer stopped before a word</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Section title="The visitor's Claude Code, paired before the chat">
        <Example
            id="chat-pairing"
            title="`<Pairing>` — a chat once Claude Code is paired"
            summary="A rep pairs their own Claude Code with the CRM. Until the bridge answers, the panel offers the click and the command that pair it; once paired, it shows the chat inside it."
            files={{
                'src/assistant/lib/ClaudeCodeChat.abide': claudeCodeChatSource,
                'src/assistant/askClaudeCode.handler.ts': askClaudeCodeSource,
                'src/assistant/permitClaudeCode.handler.ts': permitClaudeCodeSource,
                'src/assistant/lib/ClaudeCodeChat.test.ts': claudeCodeChatTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <ClaudeCodeChat />
        </Example>

        <p><code>Pairing</code> renders <code>pairing</code>'s steps: connecting, the command
            with a click that pairs, the install where no bridge app opened, and paired. What you
            put inside it renders once the bridge is paired, beside a Reconnect for a bridge that
            stopped answering. A tool the visitor's Claude Code cannot make available is named
            with it.</p>

        <p>Claude Code asks before it runs a tool its permission mode would not approve on its
            own. The prompt shows in the answer with Allow and Deny, and <code>permit</code>
            sends the answer: your handler calling <code>provider.claudeCode.permit</code>.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Styling a chat by its parts and states">
        <p>Neither component ships a style or writes a class. A class you pass lands on the
            root <code>section</code>, with every other attribute. Each element inside carries
            <code>data-part</code>, and each state is a <code>data-</code> attribute, present
            while it holds or valued where it has more than two.</p>

        <Snippet source={assistantThreadSource} path="src/assistant/lib/AssistantThread.abide"
            from={['<Chat ask=']} />

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th><code>Chat</code></th><th>What it is</th><th>Its states</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>the root <code>section</code></td><td>the chat</td><td><code>data-streaming</code> while an answer streams</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>transcript</code></td><td>the <code>ol</code> of turns, <code>role="log"</code>; give it a height and <code>overflow-y: auto</code> to scroll</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>turn</code></td><td>one <code>li</code></td><td><code>data-speaker</code> is <code>you</code> or <code>assistant</code>; <code>data-streaming</code> on the answer arriving; <code>data-stop</code> holds why it ended; <code>data-failed</code> where it failed</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>speaker</code></td><td>the turn's label, you or assistant</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>text</code></td><td>a run of words: a <code>p</code>, or a <code>div</code> around <code>Text</code></td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>image</code></td><td>an image the visitor sent</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>tool</code></td><td>a tool call's <code>details</code>, holding <code>tool-name</code>, <code>tool-input</code> and <code>tool-result</code></td><td><code>data-status</code> is <code>running</code>, <code>done</code> or <code>failed</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>permission</code></td><td>a prompt, holding <code>permission-name</code>, <code>permission-input</code>, <code>allow</code> and <code>deny</code></td><td><code>data-answer</code> is <code>waiting</code>, <code>allowed</code> or <code>denied</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>failure</code></td><td>the message an answer failed with</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>composer</code></td><td>the <code>form</code>, holding <code>input</code>, <code>send</code>, <code>stop</code>, and <code>attachments</code> with each <code>attachment</code> and its <code>remove</code></td><td><code>data-dragging</code> while files hover over it</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th><code>Pairing</code></th><th>What it is</th><th>Its states</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>the root <code>section</code></td><td>the pairing</td><td><code>data-step</code> is <code>connecting</code>, <code>unavailable</code>, <code>click</code>, <code>waiting</code>, <code>install</code> or <code>paired</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>message</code></td><td>what the step asks of the visitor</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>command</code></td><td>the <code>pre</code> holding the command that pairs, or the one that installs the bridge app</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>copy</code></td><td>copies the command</td><td><code>data-copied</code> once it has</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>pair</code></td><td>pairs with a click, or reconnects once paired</td><td></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>missing</code></td><td>the tools the paired Claude Code cannot use</td><td></td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>Target a part with an attribute selector, <code>[data-part=turn][data-speaker=you]</code>
            in a stylesheet, or from the root with a Tailwind arbitrary variant, as
            <code>[&amp;_[data-part=transcript]]:p-0</code> does in the CRM's chat. A state on the
            root is a variant of its own: <code>data-streaming:opacity-90</code>.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
